    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498-a1">

                <pb facs="0577" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg497"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne to Mr. Choate</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I referred to His Majesty’s
                    secretary of state for war your note of the 15th ultimo asking what arrangements
                    His Majesty’s Government proposed to make for the repatriation of the United
                    States citizens who have been detained as prisoners of war in Ceylon.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform your excellency that it is proposed to send these men
                    to the United States by the first packet and that until they arrive at their
                    destination they will continue to receive subsistence from His Majesty’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
